<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Trimmer roots for the browser host.

  PublishTrimmed is on (Docs/Standalone/M2-Scouting.md section 2), and a full trim is right for everything a browser
  never reaches - the six hundred kilobytes of NowUI controls, inspector, docking, markdown and code editor that the
  quick-start scene does not touch are correctly removed. What a full trim CANNOT see is the handful of members the
  shim reaches by NAME, and every one of them is here:

    the six ScriptableObject subclasses   UnityEngine.ScriptableObject.CreateInstance activates the type through
                                          Activator and dispatches Awake / OnEnable / OnDisable / OnDestroy by name
                                          (Standalone/NowUI.Engine/Object/ScriptableObject.cs:48 and :140). Those four
                                          methods are private and nothing calls them statically, so a full trim
                                          removes them and the object's lifecycle silently stops running -
                                          NowFont.OnDisable (NowFont.cs:1649) is the one that matters here, since the
                                          page bakes a font atlas. Preserved whole rather than method-by-method
                                          because the reflection is by name and a rename would not be caught.

    UnityEngine.Shader                    WebResourceProvider mints one through the shim's internal
                                          Shader(string, NowShaderInfo) constructor, by reflection, because NowUI.Web
                                          is not a friend assembly. The [DynamicDependency] on
                                          WebResourceProvider.NewShader states the same thing; this is belt and
                                          braces, and it costs a few hundred bytes.

  MEASURED, not guessed. Publishing the host three ways (placeholder backend, Release, brotli, framework + managed +
  page, fixtures excluded):

      no descriptor at all                      1167 KB   - and NowFont.OnDisable is gone
      this file                                 1275 KB
      whole NowUI.Runtime + NowUI.Engine        1610 KB

  So the correctness this file buys costs 108 KB, and the lazy version of the same correctness would cost 443 KB.

  NOT rooted, deliberately: the ~40 [RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod] methods NowRuntime.ResetAll finds by reflection.
  The frame loop never calls ResetAll - neither does the standalone test host before its run - so nothing depends on
  them here. A host that ever does call ResetAll under a trimmed publish will find it a no-op, which is a real
  behaviour difference and belongs in that host's notes, not in this file's payload.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="NowUI.Runtime">
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowFontAsset" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowFont" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowFontFamily" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowThemeAsset" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowControlRenderer" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="NowUI.NowLottieAsset" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
  <assembly fullname="NowUI.Engine">
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.Shader" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
